=== fuzzy-v2 rules ===
FUZZY-V2 RULE BASE (27 rules, IF own_queue AND waiting AND opposing_queue THEN green)

R01: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is short
R02: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is short
R03: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is short
R04: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is short
R05: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is short
R06: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is short
R07: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is short
R08: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is short
R09: IF own_queue is low  AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is short
R10: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is medium
R11: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is short
R12: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is short
R13: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is medium
R14: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is medium
R15: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is short
R16: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is long
R17: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is long
R18: IF own_queue is med  AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is medium
R19: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is long
R20: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is long
R21: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is short    AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is long
R22: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is long
R23: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is long
R24: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is moderate AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is long
R25: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is low  THEN green is long
R26: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is med  THEN green is long
R27: IF own_queue is high AND waiting is long     AND opposing_queue is high THEN green is long

Rule construction (so the table is explainable, not arbitrary):
  base level = own-queue level (low->short, med->medium, high->long)
  +1 level  if waiting is 'long' and own queue >= med   (a starved approach with demand clears)
  -1 level  if opposing queue is 'high' and own queue is not high   (yield to the heavier side)
  -1 level  if waiting is 'short', own is 'med' and opposing is not 'low'   (it just had green; share the cycle)
  levels clipped to [short..long].  When BOTH queues are high the rule is 'long': in saturation long greens
  waste the least time on the 3 s clearance interval.

Inference: min (AND), optional per-rule weight multiplies firing strength, max aggregation, centroid defuzzification.
Gene encoding: 12 breakpoints (a<b<c for own_queue, waiting, opposing_queue, green) + optional 27 rule weights in [0.2,1].
Default breakpoints (own, wait, opp, green):  (6,25,50), (12,55,100), (6,25,50), (15,35,55)

